        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under ambient laboratory atmosphere, Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol, 46 mg) and H2L (0.1 mmol, 43 mg) were weighed in a 20 mL sample vial. Methanol (10 mL) was added and the reagents were dissolved by heating and stirring. NaBPh4 (0.05 mmol, 17 mg) and triethylamine (0.2 mmol, 28 μL) were added into methanol (6 mL) and the solution was stirred thoroughly. The clear solution was filtered through a cotton plug and left to crystallize at room temperature overnight. Colorless crystals were collected by filtration and washed with cold methanol.",
